  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe built-in vise dialog now tells the user what \"Fit to the stock\" needs before Place, and the no-stock refusals read in plain English. Per the maintainer's note on the issue, the wording says the vise grips the **stock** (the block the part is cut from), not the imported model.\n\n- New app helper `vise_fit` (`fit` / `preview` / `has_stock` / `no_stock_message`): one derivation used by `InsertVise` and by the dialog's preview, so the two cannot disagree. The UI makes no world calls of its own beyond calling it.\n- Dialog, setup with no stock body: notice + button \"Open the Stock page\" (same click path as the browser's Stock row), Fit greyed and off with a hover reason, position rows shown, Place by position works.\n- Dialog, with a stock: one line that it grips the stock, plus where the vise lands and how far the jaws open (in the document unit); a stock wider than the vise's max opening is named up front. Place stays enabled (refusals stay refusals).\n- New `CommandError::Needs(String)`, displayed as is. It is used only for the vise (no stock / stock too wide), mod vise pair and parallels refusals; `CommandError::Invalid` and every other command's text are unchanged.\n- Browser: the Stock row's suffix reads `not set` while the setup's stock has no body.\n\n## Texts (before / after)\n\n- Vise: `vise not placed: invalid parameters: setup 'Setup1' has no stock to fit the vise to` -> `vise not placed: setup 'Setup1' has no stock yet, so there is nothing to fit the vise to - set the stock first (Stock page) - or place the vise by position instead`\n- Mod vise: `... has no stock to fit the mod vise to` (with prefix) -> `the setup has no stock yet, so there is nothing to fit the mod vise to - set the stock first (Stock page)`\n- Parallels: likewise `... nothing to fit the parallels under - set the stock first (Stock page)`\n- Dialog notice: `This setup has no stock yet. A vise grips the stock - the block the part is cut from - not the imported model. Set the stock on the Stock page to fit the vise to it, or place the vise by position below.`\n- With a stock: `Opens to 40.000 mm on the stock's Y width; the fixed jaw sits against the stock's +Y side (...), centred in X (...); the stock sits on the jaw floor (...).`\n\n## Pinned by\n\n- App: `vise_needs_stock` (`the_three_fits_name_the_missing_stock_and_the_stock_page`, `the_preview_is_the_commands_own_fit`, `a_stock_wider_than_the_vise_is_refused_up_front_and_by_the_command`).\n- UI (structural, no pixels): `fixture_vise_stock_tests` (notice, greyed Fit, Stock page button and its target, position rows, Place by position, landing line with a stock, too-wide stock, queued refusal text, `Stock  not set` row).\n- Removed `a_refused_vise_is_named_in_the_dialog` (its Place click now places by position); the refusal is covered by the queued-command test above.\n- Also run green: builtin_vise, mod_vise, mod_vise_plate, builtin_accessory, mcp_vise, mcp_mod_vise, mcp_accessory, self_centering_vise, mcp_self_centering_vise, fixtures, ui `structural`, `setup_tree`; clippy -D warnings on camcraft-app and camcraft-ui.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNot seen on screen - only the kittest harness was run (nothing launched). Layout, wrapping of the long notice and the greyed look are unverified by eye. Opening the Stock page for a dialog setup other than the active one activates it, as the browser row does. No snapshot PNG touched. Decisions: `docs/decisions/1105-vise-needs-stock.md`.\n\nChangelog: The built-in vise dialog says a setup needs its stock before a fit and where the vise will land; the no-stock refusals read in plain English; the browser shows `Stock  not set` (#1105, PR #1111)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1105\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
